.TH buffer_default 3
.SH NAME
buffer_default \- initialize a buffer structure with default values
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include "buffer.h"

void buffer_default(buffer* \fIb\fP, buffer_op_fn* \fIop\fP);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B buffer_default
initializes the provided
.I buffer
structure
.I b
by setting its file descriptor to -1 and its internal pointers and counters to zero.
It assigns the provided function pointer
.I op
as the buffer's operation handler.

This is typically used as the first step in setting up a buffer before
calling other buffer manipulation functions.
.SH SEE ALSO
buffer_init(3)